# GDM reads the greeter logo from a separate dconf profile ("gdm"). Without
# this keyfile, gnome-shell falls back to the schema default
# (/usr/share/pixmaps/fedora-gdm-logo.png), which fedora-logos provides and
# which is the Fedora wordmark. Utah overrides the schema string here.
#
# A pixmap overlay also exists: common ships a Bluefin-branded
# system_files/bluefin/usr/share/pixmaps/fedora-gdm-logo.png, copied into
# the image by Containerfile:118. It is not effective because
# utah-install-packages runs after the overlay (Containerfile:148-150)
# and reinstalls fedora-logos, clobbering every /usr/share/pixmaps/fedora-*.png.
# Root-cause ticket: #398. This dconf override is the working fix and does
# not need the overlay PNG to land on disk.
#
# The image is the same bluefin-logos/bluefin.png the desktop contract asserts
# under /usr/share/ublue-os/bluefin-logos/ -- the file Common ships. Using the
# existing asset avoids duplicating a ~285 KB PNG in two places, and a single
# source means a brand refresh in Common flows to both the desktop shell and
# the greeter without a second commit here. That the PNG exists is enforced by
# the [branding].files entry in contracts/bluefin-desktop.toml, not by dconf:
# the value below is an opaque string to dconf and a dangling path compiles
# without complaint.
#
# The GDM dconf profile is provided by the gdm RPM itself
# (system-db:gdm,file-db:/usr/share/gdm/greeter-dconf-defaults); Utah only
# needs to drop a keyfile in /etc/dconf/db/gdm.d/ and let dconf-update.service
# recompile the database on first boot. The build also runs `dconf update` at
# branding time so a malformed keyfile surfaces immediately rather than at
# first boot, which is what issue #378 caught.

[org/gnome/login-screen]
logo='/usr/share/ublue-os/bluefin-logos/bluefin.png'
